---
intent: >
  Migrate the bundled default brain.aide template body from the retired
  heading-based grammar (`## Prose` / `## Playbook hub` / `## Research hub`)
  to the marker-pair grammar required by the post-pivot parseBrainAide
  (`<!-- aide-prose-start -->` / `<!-- aide-prose-end -->`,
  `<!-- aide-playbook-start -->` / `<!-- aide-playbook-end -->`,
  `<!-- aide-research-start -->` / `<!-- aide-research-end -->`). Strip the
  retired storage-specific vocabulary from the emitted prose (the template's
  body bytes carry the spec's three carve-outs only — `obsidianBrainAideTemplate`
  the helper folder, the `obsidian` MCP key in legacy migration prose, and
  the `.obsidian` directory heuristic comment elsewhere). Repoint test
  fixtures and assertions from `result.playbookHub`/`result.researchHub` to
  the renamed `result.playbook`/`result.research` typed fields. Frontmatter
  shape and platform branching are unchanged.
---

## Project Structure

This is an edit plan against an existing helper. The folder shape and
external function signature are unchanged. What changes:

- The emitted body switches from three heading-bounded sections to three
  marker-pair-bounded sections.
- Forbidden storage-specific tokens in the emitted prose body
  (`vault`, `obsidian` outside the carve-outs, `note`-as-synonym,
  `wikilink`, `hub note`, `hub`) are rewritten to storage-agnostic terms.
- Tests rename body-field assertions from `playbookHub`/`researchHub` to
  `playbook`/`research`, replace the heading-anchored regex assertions
  with marker-aware assertions, and drop assertions that asserted
  forbidden vocabulary in the prose.

```
src/service/install/provisionBrain/obsidianBrainAideTemplate/
├── plan.aide                     ← [this file, REPLACES the prior 4/4-done
│                                    plan that targeted heading-grammar +
│                                    `playbookHub`/`researchHub` field names]
├── index.ts                      ← [edit] export default function
│                                    obsidianBrainAideTemplate(rootPath: string): string
│                                    signature unchanged. Behavior changes:
│                                      - frontmatter unchanged (`name` +
│                                        platform-branched `mcpServerConfig`)
│                                      - body restructured: three marker-pair
│                                        sections in fixed order — prose,
│                                        playbook, research — replacing the
│                                        retired `## Prose` / `## Playbook hub` /
│                                        `## Research hub` headings
│                                      - prose body rewritten to use
│                                        storage-agnostic vocabulary; the
│                                        retired tokens (`vault`, `wikilink`,
│                                        `hub`, `note`-as-synonym) are
│                                        scrubbed. The MCP tool names
│                                        `mcp__brain__read_note` and
│                                        `mcp__brain__search_notes` remain
│                                        verbatim (those are tool names the
│                                        agent must call, not our prose
│                                        vocabulary)
│                                      - playbook section bytes preserve
│                                        their structural shape (H1 title,
│                                        Task Routing table skeleton, How to
│                                        Use This Index, Always Read First,
│                                        empty Sections + Contents lists)
│                                        with nested `## ` already demoted
│                                        to `### ` from the prior cycle —
│                                        the marker-pair walker is byte-based
│                                        so nested `## ` is no longer a
│                                        parser concern, but the demotion
│                                        carries forward as it reads cleaner
│                                      - research section bytes preserve
│                                        their structural shape mirroring
│                                        the playbook section
│                                      - JSDoc updated to enumerate the
│                                        marker-pair grammar and reference
│                                        `.aide/docs/brain-aide.md`
└── index.test.ts                 ← [edit] tests reflect the marker-pair
                                     grammar and the renamed `playbook` /
                                     `research` typed fields. Vocabulary
                                     sweep removes assertions that asserted
                                     forbidden tokens in the prose body
                                     (`expect(result.prose).toContain("wikilink")`
                                     and similar). Round-trip and
                                     happy-path assertions stay structurally
                                     identical, only field-name and
                                     content-anchor strings change.
```

The helper has no sub-folders and no .aide of its own — the parent
spec at `../.aide` is the governing intent for this helper's content.

## Prerequisites

**`src/service/parseBrainAide/`** must export the marker-pair grammar
already landed (24/24 in its plan, 61/61 tests green):

- `parseBrainAideFromString(content: string)` returns `{ kind: "ok",
  config, prose, playbook, research }` when the content carries exactly
  the three required marker pairs in fixed order.
- The renamed fields are `playbook` and `research` (NOT
  `playbookHub`/`researchHub`).
- A heading-based body (`## Prose` / `## Playbook hub` / `## Research
  hub` with no marker pairs) returns `{ kind: "malformed-body", reason:
  "missing markers: <!-- aide-prose-start -->, <!-- aide-prose-end -->,
  <!-- aide-playbook-start -->, <!-- aide-playbook-end -->,
  <!-- aide-research-start -->, <!-- aide-research-end -->" }`.

This prerequisite is already satisfied — no work required. The
breakage report explicitly cites the parser cascade as complete.

